## 6. Worker rules

1. After authorization, read the frozen package and code, then apply the confirmed review mode. By default, create the full-history inherited Reviewer before implementation and obtain `READY_REVIEW`; for `self_review`, record `SELF_REVIEW_READY` without a subagent.
2. Only after that readiness receipt, create an active Goal that references this file's absolute path; do not set an unrequested token budget.
3. Complete items one by one and update `execution/worker-main.md`.
4. After implementation self-check, mark the item `implemented_pending_review` and invoke the configured review mode.
5. Mark `approved` only after an exact `REVIEW` or `SELF` approval receipt.
6. Reviewer findings follow the risk-proportional gate: supported business paths and high-consequence invariants may block; speculative long-tail hardening is recorded as non-blocking residual work.
7. After all items pass, complete each part audit and final consistency checks.

